    "result_text": "All tests pass \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`, 3/3 green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI added an optional, validated, lower-cased `email` field to owners. Since only `POST /api/owners` and `GET /api/owners/{id}` are exercised by the tests, but the spec is stated generally (\"an owner may include email\"), I wired it consistently through both the create and update paths.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added an optional `email` property (`format: email`, `maxLength: 255`, not in `required`) to the `OwnerFields` schema. This regenerates `OwnerFieldsDto`/`OwnerDto` with `email` getters/setters.\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added an `email` column with getter/setter (nullable; no `@NotEmpty`).\n\n3. **Database schemas** \u2014 added an `email` column to all four `schema.sql` files (hsqldb/h2/mysql/postgres). Tests use hsqldb with `ddl-auto=none`, so the DDL had to be explicit.\n\n4. **`data.sql`** (hsqldb, mysql) \u2014 the seed inserts used positional `INSERT INTO owners VALUES (...)`, which broke on the new column; switched them to explicit column lists. (h2/postgres already listed columns.)\n\n5. **`OwnerEmail.java`** (new) \u2014 shared normalizer: null/blank \u2192 absent (`null`); present \u2192 syntactic check (`^[^@\\s]+@[^@\\s]+\\.[^@\\s]+$`), throwing on invalid, else returning the trimmed, lower-cased value.\n\n6. **`InvalidEmailException` + handler + escalation YAML** (new) \u2014 mirrors the existing telephone escalation, responding `400` with `{\"errors\":[\"email\"]}`.\n\n7. **Validation wiring** \u2014 `ValidateOwnerFields` (POST) and `ValidateOwner` (PUT) call `OwnerEmail.normalize` and write the result back; `ApplyOwner` (PUT) now copies `email` onto the entity. MapStruct maps `email` by name automatically for the create path and the responses.\n\nBehavior: missing email \u2192 accepted; `Test.User@Example.COM` \u2192 stored/returned as `test.user@example.com`; `not-an-email` \u2192 `400`.",
